    "Notes Updated": "3/25/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Spring Training impression: Wow\n Starter now?\n Came into spring going from a 2 pitch guy to a 5 pitch guy, all of which are interesting\n Four Seam is an absurd shape and was showing a VAA of around -3.6 in his statcast outing, in the mid 90's, should miss a ton of bats up in the zone and above\n \"Cutter\" is more of a gyro slider in my opinion in the 87-89 range with very good feel for commanding it\n Changeup is pretty high spin, but gets a ton of armside run in the 86-87 range\n Sweeper in the low 80's is a really nice looking pitch\n Also showed a sinker that has a decent shape\n The 4S and CT/SL are the two best pitches still, but he has rounded out a repertoire that allows him to start and should be in the T-Rats rotation to start 2025",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/28/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "DRAFT REPORT\n Reliever\n Two pitch pitcher, Hardin’s calling card is a mid 90s fastball with a ton of horizontal run, which he can run up to 97 MPH. \n Coming from his low arm slot, the fastball has a really interesting shape to it\n Other pitch is a mid 80s slider that could use some improvement in its consistency\n Fastball will carry the profile\n Command seemingly needs work as well",
